    "result_text": "All 11 tests pass. The change is complete and green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required an owner's `displayName` to be returned formatted exactly as `LastName, FirstName` from the stored names. Since owners are serialized through the OpenAPI-generated `OwnerDto` (shared by both the create/POST responder and the GET endpoint), I made two changes:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a `readOnly` `displayName` string property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` on `toOwnerDto` that computes `displayName` via the expression `owner.getLastName() + \", \" + owner.getFirstName()`, sourcing it from the stored entity names.\n\nNo new function classes or endpoint YAML were needed \u2014 the value flows through the existing `RespondWithOwnerCreated` responder (and every other owner response) via the mapper. The full suite (11 tests, including the new `Cp05Tests`) is green.",
